{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_125a7378bdac48a788b942e00953a85a","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"/mnt/afs/panzhengyuan/llm_training/project/rate_website_figma-sft-cc-tap/storage/local-runtime/model-local-a282d9c9a73446c8/ckpt-270-shadow","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm reviewing the 11 frames I need to build at 414×932, noting the brand color and fonts, plus the existing components like buttons, text fields, and the shell elements.\n\nMy plan is to set up reusable components first (icon tints, bottom nav, cards), then build out each frame using them, finishing with prototype links between screens. I'll work through this with a setup call that establishes the page and components before tackling the individual frames.\n\nSince each code block runs in its own context, I'll need to redefine compact helper functions in every call. I'm also working out how to recolor icon instances by traversing their children and overriding stroke/fill paints, and confirming I can reuse the existing 03 Workspace page rather than creating a new one.\n\nNow I'm sketching out the design system: a light neutral palette with specific surface, text, and status colors, along with a type scale using DM Sans for headings/numbers and Inter for body text, plus consistent radii and spacing values. I'm also mapping out the frame layout, starting with a primary-filled Splash screen.\n\nI'm planning each screen's structure: a centered logo tile on Splash, then a Welcome screen with illustration, copy, and a \"Create account\" button, followed by Create Account screens in empty/filled/error states, a scrollable Home screen with greeting, portfolio card, plans carousel, and article list, and finally a My_Asset_Overlay showing a dimmed Home behind a bottom sheet.\n\nNow I'm continuing with the remaining screens — a notification list, profile with avatar and entry list, contact info, and bank account info — along with bottom navigation for Home/Account and a shared status bar component.\n\nI'm planning to create two bottom nav variants as components and thinking through how to structure component creation: rather than manually building component nodes, I can wrap frames with `figma.createComponentFromNode` after laying out the nav content.\n\nI'm deciding to build each component inside the 03_Workspace page itself, since that's the allowed delivery location, and planning to arrange the eleven frames in a row spaced 480px apart starting from x=0, keeping everything in a single page for simpler prototype linking.\n\nMy approach is to first make one setup call that creates the reusable components (bottom nav, plan card, article card, list row, history row, notification row, bank card, and state variants of the text field), then follow with one call per frame to build out the actual screens, and finish with a final call to wire up the prototype connections.\n\nI'm narrowing the component list down to just the essentials — bottom nav for home/account, a plan card, article card, list row with icon/title/chevron, history row, notification row, and bank card — while treating text field states as per-frame styling instead of separate components to keep things manageable.\n\nWriting helper code...\n\nI'm reconsidering the default fills on created frames and planning a compact helper function for text that handles font loading and styling in one call.\n\nNow I'm designing the bottom navigation component with four tabs, using horizontal auto layout with padding, and mapping out which icons to use for Product and Transaction tabs from the available icon set.\n\nI'm setting active tab colors—primary green for the active state, a lighter gray for inactive—and planning to build two variants, one with Home active and one with Account active, before starting to construct the nav component itself.\n\nAdding a top divider stroke, then I'll convert the finished frame into a component using the API, placing it on the current workspace page with a descriptive name like \"BottomNav/Home_Active\".\n\nI'm working through the component creation order—creating the component first, then appending the frame as a child so its layout persists, then removing the original frame. Now I'll write out the component list for the first call: BottomNav with Home and Account variants, a PlanCard component, and an ArticleCard component, sized to fit the width constraints.\n\nRounding out the remaining components: ListRow, HistoryRow, NotificationRow, and BankCard, each with their own width and icon/label structure. For ListRow, I'll set the icon as an instance override rather than hardcoding it, so the component stays reusable across different list contexts.\n\nI'm also mapping out the icon component keys for each entry type — bank account, contact info, document, settings, and source of funding — so I can swap them in dynamically. Now I'm ready to start writing the first call's code.\n\nI need a helper function that finds an icon component by its name, creates an instance, and recolors its strokes and fills to match the palette. Writing icon helper...\n\nFinishing the recolor function to apply color to strokes and fills, then starting the bottom nav component setup...\n\nAdding nav items for Product and Transaction tabs, then writing a utility function to convert frames into components while preserving position. I'll plan to build a handful of card components similarly, keeping each one compact.\n\nNow sketching the PlanCard layout with horizontal auto layout, padding, gap, centered items, rounded corners, and a coin image alongside a name and return-rate text block.\n\nBuilding out the article card thumbnail, list row with icon and chevron, history row with action badge and stock price column, and starting the notification row structure...\n\nI'll build these as six components across a few calls, then move to frames. For the frames, I'm planning a 414×932 frame with a status bar instance, content area, and nav bar, keeping in mind that Home may need scrolling.\n\nFor 04_Home, I'll set it taller (1400px) to fit scrollable content — the bottom nav stays pinned at the bottom and the home indicator sits below it. Other frames stay at the standard 932 height, with the home indicator near the bottom.\n</think>\n\nReasoning summary: 已读取全部参考页面信息（品牌色 #31A062、字体 DM Sans/Inter、默认组件与媒体资产 ID）。现在开始构建：第一步在 03·Workspace 中创建可复用组件（底部导航、计划卡、文章卡、列表行等）。\n</think>\n\n"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":23314,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"76699855-d304-4fda-983c-5359f7738e40","uuid":"557d812b-638c-43c5-9096-c211bee74828","timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:45:54.245Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_125a7378bdac48a788b942e00953a85a","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"/mnt/afs/panzhengyuan/llm_training/project/rate_website_figma-sft-cc-tap/storage/local-runtime/model-local-a282d9c9a73446c8/ckpt-270-shadow","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_ff52bd616bf24e449f2ee387","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"code":"\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('2005:2'));\nawait Promise.all(['Regular','Medium','Semi Bold','Bold'].map(s=>figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Inter',style:s})).concat(['Regular','Medium','Bold'].map(s=>figma.loadFontAsync({family:'DM Sans',style:s}))));\n\nconst C={p:'#31A062',t1:'#101613',t2:'#5F6B66',t3:'#9AA5A0',surf:'#F4F7F5',line:'#E4E9E6',white:'#FFFFFF'};\nfunction hex(h){h=h.replace('#','');return{r:parseInt(h.slice(0,2),16)/255,g:parseInt(h.slice(2,4),16)/255,b:parseInt(h.slice(4,6),16)/255};}\nfunction S(h,o){return[{type:'SOLID',color:hex(h),opacity:o===undefined?1:o}];}\nfunction txt(ch,size,style,fam,color,lh){const t=figma.createText();t.fontName={family:fam||'Inter',style:style||'Regular'};t.characters=ch;t.fontSize=size;t.fills=S(color||C.t1);t.lineHeight={value:lh||Math.round(size*1.45),unit:'PIXELS'};return t;}\nfunction recolor(n,c){if('strokes' in n&&n.strokes.length)n.strokes=S(c);if('fills' in n&&n.fills!==figma.mixed&&Array.isArray(n.fills)&&n.fills.length)n.fills=S(c);if('children' in n)n.children.forEach(k=>recolor(k,c));}\nasync function icon(name,size,color){const c=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(name);const i=c.createInstance();recolor(i,color);if(size!==24)i.rescale(size/24);return i;}\n\n// ---------- Bottom nav component ----------\nasync function nav(active){\n  const f=figma.createFrame();f.name='BottomNav';f.resize(414,74);f.fills=S(C.white);\n  f.layoutMode='HORIZONTAL';f.paddingTop=12;f.paddingBottom=14;f.itemSpacing=0;f.counterAxisAlignItems='CENTER';\n  f.strokes=S(C.line);f.strokeAlign='INSIDE';f.strokeTopWeight=1;f.strokeBottomWeight=0;f.strokeLeftWeight=0;f.strokeRightWeight=0;\n  const items=[['Home','6:269'],['Product','6:270'],['Transaction','6:271'],['Account','6:272']];\n  for(const [label,id] of items){\n    const on=label===active;const col=on?C.p:C.t3;\n    const it=figma.createFrame();it.name='tab_'+label;it.fills=[];it.layoutMode='VERTICAL';it.itemSpacing=5;\n    it.counterAxisAlignItems='CENTER';it.primaryAxisAlignItems='CENTER';\n    f.appendChild(it);it.layoutGrow=1;it.layoutAlign='STRETCH';\n    const ic=await icon(id,22,col);it.appendChild(ic);\n    const tl=txt(label,11,on?'Semi Bold':'Regular','Inter',col,14);tl.name='label';it.appendChild(tl);\n  }\n  const comp=figma.createComponent();comp.resize(414,74);comp.fills=[];\n  comp.appendChild(f);f.x=0;f.y=0;\n  comp.name='BottomNav/'+active;\n  f.remove();\n  return comp;\n}\nconst navHome=await nav('Home');navHome.x=0;navHome.y=1800;\nconst navAccount=await nav('Account');navAccount.x=460;navAccount.y=1800;\n\n// ---------- PlanCard ----------\nasync function planCard(coinId,name,ret){\n  const f=figma.createFrame();f.name='PlanCard';f.resize(120,140);f.fills=S(C.white);\n  f.cornerRadius=16;f.strokes=S(C.line);f.strokeWeight=1;\n  f.layoutMode='VERTICAL';f.paddingTop=12;f.paddingBottom=12;f.paddingLeft=10;f.paddingRight=10;\n  f.itemSpacing=6;f.counterAxisAlignItems='CENTER';f.primaryAxisAlignItems='CENTER';\n  const coin=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(coinId);const ci=coin.createInstance();ci.resize(56,56);f.appendChild(ci);\n  const n=txt(name,14,'Semi Bold','DM Sans',C.t1,18);n.name='plan_name';f.appendChild(n);\n  const r=txt(ret+' return',11,'Medium','Inter',C.p,15);r.name='plan_return';f.appendChild(r);\n  const c=figma.createComponent();c.resize(120,140);c.fills=[];c.appendChild(f);f.x=0;f.y=0;f.remove();\n  c.name='PlanCard';return c;\n}\nconst pc=await planCard('5:37','Gold','30%');pc.x=920;pc.y=1800;\n\n// ---------- ArticleCard ----------\nasync function articleCard(thumbId,title,summary){\n  const f=figma.createFram